# How this deck is invoked.  tests/bin/check_status.sh reads it; a deck with
# no .invoke is run '$(SPICE) --batch -n <deck>', which is what
# op-empty-netlist.cir -- the same six bytes -- already asserts.
#
# route stdin is 'ngspice -b -n < <deck>'.  The deck arrives on standard input
# instead of as a filename argument, which is the second of the three rows
# doc/codex/issues/0072 criterion 1 names: the same ft_cktcoms() call at
# main.c:1581, reached with no deck filename anywhere on the command line.
#
# What this file cannot do is witness itself.  The deck is the reproducer byte
# for byte and returns before any control language runs, so it cannot read
# $inputdir -- the one cp variable that separates this route from batch -- and
# the diagnostic it does produce is byte-identical on all three routes.  See
# Makefile.am's comment block and this batch's receipt 02.
route stdin
